        "For students applying overseas instead, the IB Diploma travels well by design — that's part of its original purpose — and A Level results are read directly by universities in the UK, several Commonwealth countries and beyond. A student who completed IGCSE at a Philippine school and moved into A Level or DP afterward is following a well-understood pathway internationally, and admissions offices abroad are generally familiar with reading Philippine-based international-school transcripts alongside ones from anywhere else.",
